{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS8JPnC9fXYk4VqTCvA5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I found both causes and fixed them, and they're written up in `ANSWER.md`. launchd has been running the job every night (`runs = 6`, `last exit code = 1`), but the script fails and then dies before it can tell you.\n\n1. **\"Not logged in\":** the plist sets only `PATH`, so `USER` isn't set under launchd. Without it, `claude -p` can't find its keychain login and fails immediately, every run. I added `USER` and `LOGNAME` to the plist.\n2. **`status=$?`:** in zsh, `status` is read-only, and assigning to it kills the script at line 19. The failure notification comes after that line, so it never ran, which is why you got nothing at all. I changed it to `rc=$?`.\n\nI also hardened the script so it can't go quiet like this again:\n- It sends a notification if it dies unexpectedly anywhere.\n- It logs `USER`, claude's exit code and how long each run took.\n- It counts an empty output file as a failure even if claude exits 0.\n- `claude` gets a closed stdin (`< /dev/null`).\n- `notify.sh` now uses `curl -f`, so Telegram API errors show up in the log.\n\n**Testing:** I only tested with stand-in `claude` and `notify.sh` scripts. Each of the four paths (fails, succeeds, exits 0 with empty output, and the old `status=` line put back) sent exactly one notification. I haven't run it under real launchd or against Telegram. That's for you on the Mac: unload and reload the plist (`launchctl bootout` then `bootstrap`), run it once with `launchctl kickstart -k`, check the results, then break it once on purpose; the exact commands are in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n**From your colleague's note,** these parts applied: check `launchctl print` first, read the stderr log, the read-only `status`, setting `USER` for \"Not logged in\", and not trusting the exit code alone. The \"pipe the prompt via stdin\" fix didn't: your prompt arrived fine. I only added `< /dev/null` as a precaution."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2277,"cache_read_input_tokens":27830,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2277},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eca78621-a076-4eda-a445-bfb69f05c9c8","uuid":"8e2bec04-81d8-4399-85e8-9f5f6f5821e7","timestamp":"2026-10-27T04:40:34.637Z","request_id":"req_011CgS8JPYZH7BxJh3mbYDNf"}
